```plaintext
0result.sql
```

Reason:  
0result.sql joins to the ORDERS table and explicitly removes rows whose parent order was either Cancelled or Returned, satisfying the requirement to “exclude any products associated with orders that were canceled or returned.”  
1result.sql filters only on ORDER_ITEMS and never references ORDERS, so items that belong to a cancelled / returned order—but whose individual row status is not set to “Cancelled/Returned”—would still be included, violating the specification.